From: xxxvik-xakerxxx <xxxviktor.lyskoxxx@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] pinctrl: mediatek: mt6878: fill holes in EINT table

The MT6878 EINT descriptor array jumps directly from interrupt 116 to 196.
The common EINT code indexes this array by hardware interrupt number up to
ap_num, so interrupt 212 reads past the end of the array and is left with
no irqchip.  This prevents the PMIF SPMI controller from requesting its
RCS interrupt and consequently blocks the MT6363 PMIC and its regulators.

Represent the unused EINT numbers explicitly, as done by newer MediaTek
pinctrl tables, so the array remains directly indexable.

Signed-off-by: xxxvik-xakerxxx <xxxviktor.lyskoxxx@gmail.com>

---
 drivers/pinctrl/mediatek/pinctrl-mtk-mt6878.h | 81 +++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 81 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/pinctrl/mediatek/pinctrl-mtk-mt6878.h b/drivers/pinctrl/mediatek/pinctrl-mtk-mt6878.h
index e4262ce84..4bd08b946 100644
